{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Upon their slain.</b> With their slain. Examples: ״על שדה הארץ יחשב״, ״על עולת התמיד״, ״האנשים על הנשים״, ״על כרעיו ועל קרבו״, ״על פרשה״, ״על כל קרבנך״." "<b>And Balaam.</b> After he returned to his place, to Aram Naharaim, he came again to Midian to take money from the elders of Midian, when he heard word of the plague that had struck Israel through his counsel. Another interpretation: because he had told them ״לא הביט און״ etc. — meaning, they had not sinned, so why should he refrain from blessing them? They arose and caused them to sin, and they sent to him: now you will be able to curse them, for they have sinned — and he came and was killed."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:21.618465404Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}